# Continued fractions and the Farey structure of the rationals, the arithmetic of best approximation. Writing a number as
# an integer plus one over an integer plus one over another peels off its nested self-similarity, and truncating gives the
# convergents, the fractions that approximate it better than any with a smaller denominator. The golden ratio has the
# simplest continued fraction of all, every layer a one, so it is approached the most slowly and is the most irrational
# number, and its convergents are exactly the ratios of consecutive Fibonacci numbers. This file DEFINES the Fibonacci
# sequence whose ratios are the golden convergents and PROVES its recurrence, then records as machine-integer facts the
# unimodular relation of a Farey pair, the mediant construction of the Stern-Brocot tree, and the Cassini identity that
# makes consecutive Fibonacci convergents best approximations.

# A natural number, zero or a successor.
form natural
  case zero
  case succ
    link prior, like natural

# Addition, to sum consecutive convergent numerators.
task plus
  take a, like natural
  take b, like natural
  like natural
  fork case, read a
    case zero
      send back
        read b
    case succ
      send back
        make succ
          bind prior
            call plus
              read prior
              read b

# The Fibonacci sequence, whose consecutive ratios are the convergents of the golden ratio's continued fraction.
task fib
  take n, like natural
  like natural
  fork case, read n
    case zero
      send back
        make zero
    case succ
      link m
      fork case, read m
        case zero
          send back
            make succ
              bind prior
                make zero
        case succ
          link k
          send back
            call plus
              call fib
                read m
              call fib
                read k

# THE CONVERGENT RECURRENCE: the Fibonacci numerators grow by fib (n+2) = fib (n+1) + fib n, the same recurrence the
# continued-fraction convergents of the golden ratio obey, for every n. Proved definitionally for every index.
rule the-convergent-recurrence
  seat n, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call fib
        make succ
          bind prior
            make succ
              bind prior
                read n
      call plus
        call fib
          make succ
            bind prior
              read n
        call fib
          read n
  calm hold

# FAREY NEIGHBORS are unimodular: one half and two thirds satisfy the cross difference 2 * 2 - 1 * 3 = 4 - 3 = 1, so their
# Ford circles are tangent and no fraction of smaller denominator lies between them.
hold farey-neighbors-are-unimodular
  call is-equal
    code 1
    call subtract
      call multiply
        code 2
        code 2
      call multiply
        code 1
        code 3

# THE MEDIANT of one half and one over one is two thirds, numerators adding and denominators adding: numerator 1 + 1 = 2,
# denominator 2 + 1 = 3, the Stern-Brocot child between the two parents.
hold mediant-numerator-adds
  call is-equal
    code 2
    call add
      code 1
      code 1

# CASSINI at consecutive Fibonacci convergents five thirds and eight fifths: 5 * 5 - 8 * 3 = 25 - 24 = 1, the unimodular
# gap that makes each the best rational approximation at its size.
hold golden-convergents-are-unimodular
  call is-equal
    code 1
    call subtract
      call multiply
        code 5
        code 5
      call multiply
        code 8
        code 3
